                },
                {
                    "file": "common/src/host_power.cpp",
                    "line": 48,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Please avoid [PWR] from all over the code. I already commented in other PRs as well. This is not a standard practice for the messages."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/src/host_power.cpp",
                    "line": 48,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/src/host_power.cpp",
                    "line": 50,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Why this sleep? And how do you know this is good or sufficient enough number?\n\nAs an alternative solution \n1. Wouldn't it be better to move this sleep down at line 54 where you can add some retry logic, lets say 3 times for 10 secs to get the current_host_state() and compare it with expected. I know it wouldn't be ideal but it will be better than what is being used.\n2. As an ideal solution, it will be better to start relying on the PropertyChanged Signal above to trigger next set of actions after a transition has taken affect, isn't it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/src/host_power.cpp",
                    "line": 50,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Why this sleep? \n\nAfter requesting the power state transition, we need to allow for some time for it to happen. Yes, the number is arbitrary, but we cannot wait forever. So we will need some timeout value.\n\n> As an ideal solution, it will be better to start relying on the PropertyChanged Signal above to trigger next set of actions after a transition has taken affect, isn't it?\n\nYes, but then we would probably need to run a timer in parallel to it in case the value does not change.\n\nChoosing the option 1 for now, to query the host state in a loop.\nMade a loop with 10 iterations for 3 seconds each, so our maximum delay here will be 3 seconds and it will still have the maximum timeout of 30s as you suggested.\n\nIf that is too much for some use-cases, we can later switch to using PropertyChanged."
                },
                {
